// Seed part 5: initial weights (design section 6, part 5; runtime.md section 8).
//
// The starting weight of every feature template before any learning, frozen for arm A. Sense
// frequency, words used, wanted kind, shape fit and, in stage two, reached an act and unworked at
// 1; every other template at 0. ReachedAct is the strong prior toward the executable reading,
// named so it can be ablated. Unworked counts expressions left that no reading applied to (its
// value is minus that count), so a reading that reads every word beats one that leaves one.
// CandidateSource is 1 too: a token read as said scores above one read as a spelling correction a
// distance away, which otherwise counted the same as the word itself ("browser" read as "browse").
// ChecksWouldPass is 0.5: of two readings that read the same words and both act, the one whose
// dry run was checked and passed (reading a file that is there) beats one that could not be
// checked (saying its name), by less than a word read.

Pack(name="seed-weights", version="0.1.0", from=Seed("weights"))

// Stage one (runtime.md section 8.1)
Concept(WordsUsed(), Weight(1))
Concept(WantedKind(), Weight(1))
Concept(ShapeFit(), Weight(1))
Concept(SenseFrequency(), Weight(1))
Concept(CandidateSource(), Weight(1))
Concept(WordFrequency(), Weight(0.25))
Concept(Neighbour(), Weight(0))
Concept(Evidence(), Weight(0))
Concept(Match(), Weight(0))
Concept(Unmatched(), Weight(0.25))
Concept(Trust(), Weight(0))
Concept(Coverage(), Weight(0))
Concept(FocusSource(), Weight(0))
Concept(FocusFit(), Weight(0.25))

// The scored match (runtime.md 6.2): its features are costs (an exact match costs nothing),
// weighed one by one, apart from the Match template's own weight (Match:Said, in choosing a
// referent, stays at 0). A match whose score is below the threshold is not a candidate.
Fact(Feature(), Weight("Match:Uncovered", 1))
Fact(Feature(), Weight("Match:Unexplained", 1))
Fact(Feature(), Weight("Match:Distance", 0.25))
Concept(Match(), Threshold(-0.5))

// A reading the user gave (trust level 1) is what they said they mean (runtime.md 8.1: Trust):
// it outweighs the guesses (a sense, a frame) that would read the same words, and the steps of
// its meaning left to work out.
Fact(Feature(), Weight("Trust:1", 3))

// Stage two (runtime.md section 8.2)
Concept(ReachedAct(), Weight(1))
Concept(NeedsMet(), Weight(0))
Concept(ChecksWouldPass(), Weight(0.5))
Concept(Blocked(), Weight(0))
Concept(UnknownEffects(), Weight(0))
Concept(Unworked(), Weight(1))
